<title>PORTUGAL: Anglo-French bridge consortium sues Portugal.</title>
<headline>Anglo-French bridge consortium sues Portugal.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French consortium Lusoponte, which is building a bridge over Lisbon's river Tagus, said on Monday that it was suing the Portuguese government over the cost of land expropriation.</p>
<p>The consortium said it filed a suit before the International Commercial Court in Paris because the real costs of compensation involved were far higher than those laid down in its contract with the authorities.</p>
<p>A company spokesman told Reuters the contract put compensation at 380 million escudos when the real costs were some two billion escudos.</p>
<p>The Vasco da Gama bridge is due to be completed in 1998.</p>
<p>($1=185 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
